# inc-kgzx: photograph where "Undeath to Death" kills, under the phase-2b SRD
# rule.
#
# THE RULE, as lib/pspells.irh now states it (the live spell near line 5878):
#     aval: AR_GLOBE; lval: 4; qval: Q_TAR | Q_LOC; sval: WILL;
#     pval: (LEVEL_MAX20)d4; tval: MA_UNDEAD; Flags: EF_LIM_MTYPE, EF_HD_POOL
# A 4-square-radius burst at the aimed point; ONE pool of (caster level)d4 Hit
# Dice per cast, max 20d4, spent on the eligible undead fewest Hit Dice first,
# ties by distance to the centre; an undead of 9+ Hit Dice is skipped without
# spending or wasting the pool; leftover too small for the next creature is
# wasted; a creature's Hit Dice are subtracted BEFORE its Will save (a save
# negates the destruction but not the cost). Magic::AGlobe implements the pool;
# the save and spell resistance stay in Magic::MagicStrike's strike path.
#
# HOW IT WAS BEFORE (phase 2a, committed): aval AR_BALL, lval 3, Q_TAR, pval
# (LEVEL_1PER1)d8. The ball exploded where the shot landed and each undead
# rolled its own (caster level)d8, dying if that beat its current HP; no save.
# The ball stopped at the first creature in its path, so the only undead ever
# destroyed was D, the claw beside the caster -- see logs/inc-kgzx/after-flag/.
#
# THE SCENE. The caster (orc priest of Aiswin, character level 11 through Free
# Advancement, "Undeath to Death" learned through Learn Any Spell so it is
# innate and its caster level is ChallengeRating = 11) stands in the Entry
# Chamber. The corridor east is open to x+9; a wall sits at x+10. Five undead
# are summoned in that corridor with Wizard Monster Summoning, on distinct
# squares, at fixed offsets from the caster (the absolute origin moves with the
# seed, the offsets do not):
#
#   D  caster+1  a crawling claw, 1 HD -- RIGHT NEXT TO THE CASTER, 6 squares
#                from the aim point: outside the 4-square burst.
#   B  caster+4  a crawling claw, 1 HD -- 3 squares from the aim point: the
#                outer edge of the burst. Radius observable.
#   T  caster+7  a crawling claw, 1 HD -- THE AIMED TARGET.
#   K  caster+8  a bodak, 9 HD (lib/mon3.irh:3422) -- 1 square from the aim
#                point: inside the burst, but at the cap, so it is skipped. Cap
#                observable.
#
# Freeze Monsters (armed in the shared setup) keeps all five on their squares
# while the screens are photographed; Wizard Sight makes the far end of the
# corridor perceivable so the target prompt accepts T and K.
#
# THE TARGET PROMPT. qval is Q_TAR | Q_LOC, and OPT_SELECT_JUMP is on, so the
# cursor opens in target mode (src/Term.cpp:2221) on a ring of candidates
# ordered by bearing from the player; these creatures all lie due east, so the
# ring order is by distance. The first RIGHT enters on the nearest (D, +1), then
# RIGHT steps to B (+4), then to T (+7), then to K (+8). Three RIGHTs confirm on
# the aimed target T; ENTER makes e.isLoc false and the burst centres on
# e.ETarget's square, which Magic::AGlobe reads at src/Magic.cpp:1547-1550.
# (INCURSION_TARGET_PROBE=1 records the chosen square; tools/check_undeath_to_death.sh
# checks it against caster+7.)
#
# Run:
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR="$PWD/logs/inc-kgzx/after-srd/seed-1" \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/undeath-to-death-area.keys 1
@include undeath-to-death-setup.keys

# --- SUMMON D, THE CLAW BESIDE THE CASTER (CASTER+1) ------------------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
TAB
@choose "Zombies"
@choose "crawling claw"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:summon-d

# --- SUMMON B, THE CLAW THREE SQUARES FROM THE AIM POINT (CASTER+4) ---------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
TAB
@choose "Zombies"
@choose "crawling claw"
RIGHT*4
ENTER
@dump:summon-b

# --- SUMMON T, THE AIMED TARGET (CASTER+7) ----------------------------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
TAB
@choose "Zombies"
@choose "crawling claw"
RIGHT*7
ENTER
@dump:summon-t

# --- SUMMON K, THE 9-HD BODAK INSIDE THE AREA (CASTER+8) --------------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Outsiders"
@choose "bodak"
RIGHT*8
ENTER
@dump:summon-k

# --- CAST UNDEATH TO DEATH, AIMED AT T --------------------------------------
m
@choose "Undeath to Death"
RIGHT*3
@dump:target-prompt
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-cast
v
@dump:messages
@while "Messages" ESC
@quit
